    {
      "id": "lem-maximal-algebraically-independent-subset-is-a-transcendence-basis",
      "concern": "[L1] cites the published one-variable evaluation definition along a specified map R -> S, but step 1.2 uses it for multivariable evaluation P(s_1,...,s_m,beta)=0 and step 2.1 treats P(s_1,...,s_m,Y) as a polynomial over k[S]. I did not find a cited statement on these pages upgrading [L1] to that multivariable use, so the key dependence step looks unsupported as written.",
      "severity": "would-be-fatal"
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-short-five-lemma-in-an-abelian-category",
      "concern": "Steps 1.1 and 1.2 use [L4] as if the subtraction surrogate produced equivalences y ~= y' + z and z ~= g y_0 + z_1. The cited theorem thm-chasing-rule-the-subtraction-surrogate, and its published guard remark rem-what-the-subtraction-rule-does-not-say, only guarantee a member killed by the chosen morphism plus two conditional compatibility clauses. The monic and epic chases therefore rely on a stronger subtraction law than the cited result states.",
      "severity": "would-be-fatal"
    }
